> 
> In fact it is impossible. Googling for the edge of the universe
> revealed that I once wrote the following analysis:
> 
> When trying to get to "killed by touching the edge of the universe" in
> the source:
>    - you need may_pass=FALSE
>    - therefore you need Passes_walls=TRUE
>    - therefore you have to be polymorphed
>    - getting killed via losehp() while polymorphed ignores any special
>      killer-string
>   -> you revert to [racial] form or get "killed while stuck in creature
> form"
> 
> So far noone seems to have bothered fixing it.

I think it's unreachable before then, if I'm reading correctly;
it'll never occur even if you're phasing.

may_pass has to be false =>
may_passwall(x, y) has to be false =>
IS_STWALL(levl[x][y].typ) has to be true =>
IS_ROCK(levl[x][y].typ) has to be true (IS_STWALL being a subset
  of IS_ROCK)

So the "Ouch!" case will always take precedence over the "You smack
into something" case.

> Setting may_pass correctly (not behind the Passes_walls check inside
> the if-clause) will probably lead to the intended bahaviour.

I don't believe so, no. I believe the current behaviour (of its
happening to be unreachable) _is_ the intended one; it's provision for
hitting an unpassable non-wall position while phasing, of which there
are presently none (but may be added in the future).

